+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias.  The optional :rst:directive:option:`canonical`
+   option gives the expression assigned to the alias; its type names are
+   cross-referenced like annotations.  Type aliases may be documented inside
+   a class, but their descriptions do not establish a nested namespace.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      Display the expression assigned to the alias and register it as an
+      alternate target for references to the alias.
+
+      .. versionadded:: 7.4
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined.  The default value is
